        "original_id": "e20ac5de-27f1-5bd8-89e7-d14bb0c39233",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alberic II of Spoleto, Marozia, Pope Leo VII, King Hugh of Italy, Pope Sergius III, Pope John X\n- Places: Rome, Italy\n- Roles: ruler of Rome, Roman noblewoman, pope\n\nFacts:\n- Marozia, born Maria and also known as Mariuccia or Mariozza, lived from about 890 to 937.\n- Marozia was a Roman noblewoman and was the alleged mistress of Pope Sergius III.\n- Pope John X gave Marozia the unprecedented titles of \"senatrix\" and \"patricia\" of Rome.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto lived from 912 to 954.\n- In 932, Alberic II of Spoleto became ruler of Rome after deposing his mother Marozia and his stepfather, King Hugh of Italy.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto ruled Rome from 932 to 954.\n- Leo VII's election to the papacy was secured by Alberic II of Spoleto while Alberic II was ruler of Rome.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
